    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two mechanisms and a persona",
      "prov:value": "[`content-acquisition`](content-acquisition.md) decides *what channel* a\nresource comes in on — a file, a link, or a description somebody gives in\ntheir own words. This skill starts one step later, where the answer was **a\nfile**, and asks the question nothing here answered until 2026-09-30: **what\nwrites the bytes into the declared queue, and what does the writer owe?**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The answer is two, not three, and the third is a persona",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, and the measurement is the argument for the obligation rather than\nagainst it:** across both declared queues on `origin/main` (2026-09-30), **0 of\n56** files carry an intake record — 49 in `uploads/`, 7 in\n`cat-harness/uploads/`, `0` files named `intake.json`, `0` per-document\nsubdirectories, against the `uploads/<document-id>/intake.json` convention\n`document-intake` documents. So the provenance gap is not the agent route's\nalone; it is every route's. What is specific to the agent is that **for the\nother two a commit exists to go back to, and for a conversation nothing does.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Route 2 — the forge's web UI",
      "prov:value": "GitHub's **\"Add files via upload\"**. Never write the URL by hand — run\n`bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/upload-url.ts [branch]`, which composes it from\nthe declaration. A hand-written one 404'd for the owner on 2026-09-20, because\nthe declared path `uploads/` is relative to the *instance* and a forge URL\nneeds it relative to the *repository*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Route 2 — the forge's web UI",
      "prov:value": "**Two hazards, both measured over this repository's whole history on\n`origin/main`, 2026-09-30.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Route 2 — the forge's web UI",
      "prov:value": "**It commits to the path you are LOOKING at.** Of **16** `Add files via upload`\ncommits, **10** put their files at the repository root — outside any declared\nqueue — and one landed in `schemas/`. Only 5 reached a queue. A file outside the\ndeclared queue is not \"nearly there\": every consumer resolves the queue from the\ndeclaration, so it reads as absent while sitting on disk. This is bean `eq01`,\nwhich tidied one batch and said in its last line that the habit was not fixed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean eq01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Route 2 — the forge's web UI",
      "prov:value": "**What that costs, measured on the most recent one.** `c8349950fa5` added three\nPDFs to `uploads/` at 00:17. `uploads/README.md` lists every file in the queue\nand is generated, so those three rows were missing from it the moment the\ncommit landed, and `readme:subgraphs:check` — a blocking step in\n`code-quality-gates.yml` — was red on the default branch. It was repaired 27\nminutes later by `606dc86d883`, *\"Regenerate after merging main …\"*, a commit\nabout something else entirely, whose diff to that README is exactly the three\nmissing rows. **The repair landed on somebody else's change**, which is the\nsame shape `skill-registration` describes: the author who sees the failure is\nwhoever opens the next pull request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The persona — a file handed to an agent in a conversation",
      "prov:value": "**Materialise the bytes before anything else.** A file that exists only in the\nconversation exists nowhere the repository can see. Write it into the declared\nqueue under a name that will still mean something — the filenames that arrived\nthrough the web UI include `ChatGPT Image Sep 20, 2026, 08_26_47 AM.png` and\n`d1a26515-9bde-455d-84bc-2e5fc196b004.png`, and two files with names like those\nturned out to be byte-identical (bean `eq01`, sha256 `30dad51dfc691587…`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean eq01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Unsettled, and stated rather than decided",
      "prov:value": "**Which instance owns a given file.** Two declared queues exist and nothing\nstates the rule for choosing between them. Bean `eq01` was closed on the\nowner's *\"only one uploads/ needed\"* (2026-09-20) and the repository now has\ntwo — the root one is declared, so it is legitimate by declaration, and the\ndecision it contradicts was never revisited. Today the honest answer is: ask,\nor follow whatever the surrounding work already uses.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean eq01",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-routes.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Unsettled, and stated rather than decided",
      "prov:value": "**Whether an arrival should be refused when it carries no intake record.** 0 of\n56 files carry one. A gate would redden `main` on arrival, which is the\nopposite of accepting what somebody offers ([`content-acquisition`](content-acquisition.md):\n*\"do not make them follow a process to hand you something they already\nhave\"*). Whether the record is owed by the placer or minted by intake is\nundecided here, deliberately — it is a rule with a cost and the owner has not\nbeen asked."
    }
  ]
}
